<section id="home">
    <h2>Welcome to Our School</h2>

    <p>
        Ole Tipis Girls High School is a public girls' boarding
        secondary school located in Narok County, Kenya. The
        institution provides an environment where learners can
        develop their academic abilities, discover their talents
        and prepare for future responsibilities. The school serves
        learners from different backgrounds and encourages them
        to pursue their educational goals with confidence,
        discipline and determination.
    </p>

    <p>
        Education at Ole Tipis Girls High School goes beyond
        classroom learning. Learners participate in academic
        activities, sports, cultural events, clubs and other
        programmes that encourage teamwork and personal growth.
        Through these experiences, students develop communication,
        leadership, creativity and problem-solving skills that
        prepare them for life beyond school.
    </p>

    <p>
        The school community recognises the importance of
        cooperation among teachers, learners, parents, alumni
        and the Board of Management. Their combined efforts help
        create a supportive learning environment, maintain school
        standards and encourage learners to work towards
        meaningful achievements. Respect, responsibility and
        commitment are essential in building a successful
        school community.
    </p>

    <p>
        As an institution serving the community, Ole Tipis Girls
        High School aims to nurture responsible, knowledgeable
        and confident young women. By encouraging academic
        excellence, integrity, creativity and service to society,
        the school seeks to prepare learners to contribute
        positively to their families, communities and the
        development of Kenya.
    </p>
</section>

